From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:50:28 -0700
Subject: [M152] media: Validate frame and texture format in MFVEA GPU readback

Original change's description:
> media: Validate frame and texture format in MFVEA GPU readback
>
> In MediaFoundationVideoEncodeAccelerator::CopyInputSampleBufferFromGpu,
> GPU textures are read back to CPU memory via gpu::CopyD3D11TexToMem.
> This path only supports NV12 textures and copies NV12 bytes.
>
> Previously, neither the frame's pixel format nor the texture's DXGI
> format were validated in CopyInputSampleBufferFromGpu when scaling was
> skipped. Additionally, the buffer allocation and advertised length were
> derived from frame->format() rather than the actual copied NV12 size.
>
> Change-Id: I9e350b03097126a3ce43cf5dfc6030b39b4a4b30
> Fixed: 563351482
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8435965
> Commit-Queue: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
> Auto-Submit: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
> Reviewed-by: Eugene Zemtsov <eugene@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Eugene Zemtsov <eugene@chromium.org>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1702292}

(cherry picked from commit f424973cf00b08c815d50cdff42e756a150b5d89)

Bug: 565213245,563351482
Change-Id: I9e350b03097126a3ce43cf5dfc6030b39b4a4b30

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
copied_bytes on this branch was computed as width * height * 3 / 2; it
is replaced by `allocation_size` as upstream. InitializeForTesting()
does not exist on this branch, so only
SetDxgiResourceMappingRequiredForTesting() was added to the header.
media_foundation_video_encode_accelerator_win_unittest.cc does not exist
on this branch; its hunks were dropped. Windows-only code.

